# Delin /etc/fstab -- see fstab(5).
#   <file system> <mount point> <type> <options> <dump> <pass>
# Device:
#   /dev/sdaN            the Nth partition (partition line number in that storage's
#                        /parts/manifest); sda = the computer's own storage, disk drives are
#                        numbered from sdb up in ascending disk ID order
#   UUID=c<computer ID>-<partition> / UUID=d<disk ID>-<partition>
#                        mount by UUID (CC has no filesystem UUID, an ID stands in for it; the
#                        prefix separates the computer's own storage from a disk, because disk
#                        IDs and computer IDs are two independently increasing sequences and
#                        would collide)
#   /dev/ccdiskN         the whole CC native filesystem (fstype ccdisk)
# Options: defaults ro rw auto noauto nofail user users
#   noauto is not mounted at boot; nofail does not block local-fs.target when the mount fails;
#   ro/rw/user/users are parsed and then ignored (Delin's fstypes have no read-only mode and no
#   setuid).
# The root filesystem is mounted by the boot loader, it does not belong here (a duplicate entry
# is skipped).
#
# Examples (commented out by default, enable when needed):
# UUID=d0-2  /mnt/data   ext2   defaults   0 2
# /dev/sdb2  /mnt/extra  ext2   noauto     0 2
